+##### onRetry(context)
+
+Type: `Function`
+
+Callback invoked only when another attempt is going to happen, right before the wait. It receives the same `context` object as `onFailedAttempt`.
+
+Unlike `onFailedAttempt`, it is not called for the final failure, so it suits things like retry metrics.
+
+The function is called _after_ `onFailedAttempt`, `shouldConsumeRetry`, and `shouldRetry`, and is _not_ called when any of them ends the retries, nor on `AbortError` or an abort through `signal`.
+
+The function can return a promise. If it throws, all retries will be aborted and the original promise will reject with the thrown error.
+
+```js
+import pRetry from 'p-retry';
+
+const run = async () => { … };
+
+const result = await pRetry(run, {
+	onRetry: ({error, attemptNumber, retryDelay}) => {
+		metrics.increment('retries');
+	}
+});
+```
+
 ##### shouldRetry(context)
 
 Type: `Function`
